+# Courier Fair Pay Lab — Status 2026-10-27
+
+## Snapshot
+
+Branch:
+`lab/courier-fair-pay-kernel-20261027`
+
+QA:
+**13/13 PASS**
+
+Production:
+**BLOCKED / NOT WIRED**
+
+## What exists
+
+### Global kernel
+- universal policy contract;
+- Fair Pay computation;
+- paid/mobilized time separation;
+- legal floor + POG fairness floor + country activity guarantee arbitration;
+- tips and expense separation;
+- production GREEN guard.
+
+### Zone economics
+- deliveries per paid hour;
+- utilization;
+- courier cost per delivery;
+- residual contribution;
+- break-even density;
+- target density;
+- explicit worker-pay protection.
+
+### Belgium
+Adapter:
+`BE-EMPLOYEE-POG-FAIR-PAY-LAB-v0.1`
+
+State:
+DRAFT.
+
+Lab hypothesis:
+19 EUR/hour POG fairness floor on paid time.
+
+This is not a Belgian legal rate.
+
+### France
+Adapter:
+`FR-INDEPENDENT-ARPE-2026-09-01-v1`
+
+Reference mechanism:
+19 EUR/activity-hour weekly guarantee, separate from tips/expenses.
+
+## Belgium scenario runner
+
+Illustrative assumptions only:
+- employer courier cost: 30 EUR/paid hour;
+- contribution before courier: 12 EUR/delivery;
+- target residual: 2 EUR/delivery.
+
+Outputs:
+- LOW: 1.5 deliveries/h, utilization 50%, residual -120 EUR over 10 paid hours;
+- BASE: 2.5 deliveries/h, utilization 75%, break-even;
+- HIGH: 3.0 deliveries/h, utilization 85%, residual +60 EUR over 10 paid hours.
+
+The worker pay remains protected in every scenario.
+
+## Next technical tranche
+
+1. Define canonical telemetry events for:
+   - waiting start/end;
+   - required reposition start/end;
+   - mission acceptance;
+   - pickup;
+   - delivery;
+   - paid adjustment;
+   - tips;
+   - expense reimbursement.
+
+2. Map these events across Merchant + Courier + API.
+
+3. Build weekly payroll statement projection.
+
+4. Add immutable policy/version ledger.
+
+5. Build Belgium Low/Base/High sensitivity sweeps over:
+   - employer hourly cost;
+   - contribution/delivery;
+   - wait time;
+   - batching;
+   - deliveries/hour.
+
+6. Do not enable production payroll before Belgium legal gates are GREEN.
+
+## Governance sync
+
+Airtable:
+- action: `recgQh8D6upiGQpAe`
+- QA proof: `recfGhklGVJkXuhmN`
+
+PurpleCRM:
+- CSC stakeholder record updated with lab status and next consultation topics.
+
+## Doctrine
+
+A bad zone is a POG problem.
+
+It is never converted into unpaid worker time or a hidden reduction of earned pay.
